# secrets / local config
.env
# fleet.env is the PRODUCTION credentials filename - Graph client secret,
# Qualys password - and the runbook tells operators to create one. Only
# `.env` was ignored, so a fleet.env copied into a checkout for a local
# replay was committable. Added on the prod box first, upstreamed here so
# every clone gets it. `*.env.example` is unaffected: it does not end .env.
*.env
fleet.env
config.local.yaml

# build outputs
# The compiled binary shares its name with the repo, so it is easy to commit
# by accident with `git add -A`. Anchored so it cannot match the directory.
/cti-agent
# Anchored to the repo root - an unanchored "bin/" also matches nested
# directories like fleet-kit/fleet/bin/, which silently excluded the fleet's
# executables (run-digest, fleet-db, fleet-board) from being tracked.
/bin/
/dist/
*.out
*.log

# OS/editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# run outputs
*.json
# The scanner KB cache is ~17MB of generated data that changes on every
# refresh. It was tracked, so `git add -A` after a rebuild committed a new
# copy each time and bloated history for no benefit - it is rebuildable from
# the Qualys API in a few minutes.
qualys_kb_cache.json

# Generated CTI reports - these map exploitable CVEs to real hostnames and
# must never be committed. internal/report does NOT redact by default -
# REPORT_HOSTNAMES defaults to `full`, so assume a stray report names real
# machines. (This comment previously claimed the opposite.) The safe
# state is for these files to be untrackable regardless of that setting.
cti-vuln-report.md
cti-qualys-report.md
*-vuln-report.md
*-cti-report.md
reports/
digest-*.html
enriched-*.json

# Real scrub patterns name internal hosts/domains - keep them local.
# Commit scripts/scrub-patterns.txt.example instead.
scripts/scrub-patterns.txt

# Local dev-run state: reports, digests, caches, sqlite. Generated, and
# contains real findings - never commit it.
.fleet-local/

# Python build artifacts - a .pyc was committed once by a `git add -A`
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor scratch. A .swp was swept into a commit by `git add -A`,
# the same way a .pyc was - and a swap file can contain unsaved text
# from whatever was being edited.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.*.swp
.*.swo

# `task log -- ship` output. Build and test verdicts, written to a file so
# they can be read without copy-pasting a terminal. Gitignored because the
# same target will happily capture whatever it is pointed at, and the cost of
# being wrong once is a real recipient list in a public repo.
.logs/

# The FILLED-IN organisation profile. The template is committed; the real one
# describes what this organisation runs, which is reconnaissance somebody
# would otherwise have to do themselves. It lives at
# /etc/cti-agent/ORG-PROFILE.md, 0640 root:ctiagent.
#
# Committing one is not recoverable by deleting it afterwards: a push
# publishes it, and it stays in the history. Matched in any directory, since
# the natural mistake is dropping a working copy beside the template.
ORG-PROFILE.md
**/ORG-PROFILE.md
